{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Record the architectural decision behind three changes to a committed, shared store format plus a field deletion, so the mixed-version protocol and each rollback boundary are discoverable. Session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 contains the measured facts; do not re-derive them.\n\n## Approach\n\nCreate docs/adr/0059-bridge-state-format-changes.md, following the current ADR template and status conventions, and link it from docs/README.md. The ADR will cite the landed A1, A2-1, A3, and A4-2 behavior and describe A2-2 as the cutover that stops legacy writes while retaining mixed-version reads.\n\n## Required content\n\n- A2: last_get_pass relocation to get_rotation.json; A3: scalar baseline normalization; A4-2: prev_snapshot narrowing to a key set; A1: baseline_advanced_at deletion.\n- Why bridge state stays committed on the tickets branch: ephemeral GitHub-hosted runners need durable state, and epic 6c9c rejected off-branch relocation.\n- The mixed-version protocol: write new plus legacy, read chronological max(new, legacy), then stop and scrub legacy only after direct deployment evidence. Explain why max is required and first-wins is unsafe.\n- A2-2 gate: A2-1 merged; successful reconcile-bridge.yml run at a descendant SHA; explicitly refreshed host probe from a descendant build with executable/source recorded and no older process; old/new-writer self-healing oracle. Explain why no pass-record version stamp is available and why direct evidence replaces elapsed time.\n- Rollback boundaries: A2-1 reversible; A3 reversible through idempotent read-path canonicalization; A2-2 supports rollback only to A2-1-or-newer; A4-2 requires its recorded forward and reverse corpus evidence.\n- Why assignee is excluded from normalization because _assignee_candidates requires its raw shape.\n- Measured results: 12.79 KB to 1.74 KB marginal cost after A1, and 218/399 identical prev key sets; cite session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Follow an existing accepted ADR structure and use the next available sequential number, 0059 at the reviewed base.\n- Add focused documentation tests or deterministic content assertions for every required decision element if an existing ADR check seam exists; otherwise verify exact headings/terms with repository grep and review the rendered Markdown links.\n- Run make lint, make typecheck, make test, and the repository documentation/link checks available at execution time.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] docs/adr/0059-bridge-state-format-changes.md exists and enumerates A1, A2, A3, A4-2, the mixed-version max protocol, the direct-evidence A2-2 gate, and every rollback boundary. Tier: deterministic document-content check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The ADR cites 12.79 KB -> 1.74 KB, 218/399 identical prev key sets, and session log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4. Tier: deterministic document-content check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The ADR explains committed-on-branch durability and why assignee remains raw. Tier: deterministic document-content check.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] docs/README.md links the ADR and the target resolves. Tier: repository link check.\n\n## Files\n\ndocs/adr/0059-bridge-state-format-changes.md; docs/README.md.\n\nScope: S. Depends on closed A3 and A4-2."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785804769166980001,"uuid":"b2610787-409e-414b-b0b3-82e44932adfd"}